From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8350: keep the primary USB GDSC in retention

The ROG Phone 5's side USB-C port (usb_1) runs as a host for hubs. With a
hub attached, every s2idle cycle collapsed usb30_prim_gdsc: on resume the
xHCI fetched from stale IOVAs (~31k SMMU context faults from SID 0x0),
reported "Host System Error", and the hub never re-enumerated until the
xHCI was rebound. This is the same failure 0090 fixed for usb_2.

Declare usb30_prim_gdsc PWRSTS_RET_ON too, so genpd leaves the controller
in retention across system suspend.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c
@@ -3453,7 +3453,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb30_prim_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc usb30_sec_gdsc = {
